/P 153 0 R
/T (HomiQ manages multiple hospitality properties through a combination of Online Travel Agencies \(OTAs\) and direct booking channels. Although the business continues to grow, property performance varies significantly in terms of revenue, occupancy, and profitability. Seasonal demand, OTA dependency, and differences in operational efficiency create challenges in identifying the most effective growth strategy. This analysis evaluates property performance, booking trends, distribution channels, and customer segments to uncover actionable recommendations that improve both revenue and profitability.)
/E (HomiQ manages multiple hospitality properties through a combination of Online Travel Agencies \(OTAs\) and direct booking channels. Although the business continues to grow, property performance varies significantly in terms of revenue, occupancy, and profitability. Seasonal demand, OTA dependency, and differences in operational efficiency create challenges in identifying the most effective growth strategy. This analysis evaluates property performance, booking trends, distribution channels, and customer segments to uncover actionable recommendations that improve both revenue and profitability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
